  "summary": "I started working in the Information Technology industry in 1987.  I currently am a Business Intelligence Web Developer with BearingPoint, working as a government contractor for the DoD.  From 1998 to 2007, I worked with developing and supporting complex web-based IBM Lotus Notes and Domino applications.  From 2001 to 2007 I was a Lotus Notes Developer/Administrator for Honeywell International, supporting the needs of the Atlantic Fleet by working on CAS for NETWARCOM. \n\nServers:  Win2000/NT, Linux/UNIX, IBM AS400, Apple Xserver, SunOne.\n\nServer Software Experience: Domino, Apache, MS IIS, Macromedia Coldfusion, J2EE.\n\nDatabase Applications: Cognos, Lotus Sametime, QuickPlace Domino.Doc, Team Studio, Domino Workflow, MS Access, WebSphere.\n\nProgramming Languages: LotusScript, JAVA, HTML, DHTML, JavaScript, Formula Language, XML, Java Applets.  \n\nGraphic Programs: Macromedia Products; Flash, Dreamweaver, Fireworks, Freehand, Adobe Photoshop.\n\nOperating Systems:  All Microsoft Windows versions, Linux RedHat and Mandrake, Sun MicroSystems, Mac OS X.\n\nSpecialties: Cognos 8 Suite\nLotus Notes and Domino Development and Administration \nWeb 2.0 Technologies\nWorkflow Application Architecture and Development\nCISSP Trained in Information Assurance\nSix Sigma Green Belt Certified\nU.S. Government Secret Security Clearance",
